==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Li'l Mythical Titan''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Li'l Jamiera Cat''' when obtained from [[Tiny Fists (Deadly)|Li'l Titan Awakens!]] and is level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
==='''Normal/Evolved Form'''===
Due to being the Li'l version of a [[:Category:Normal Cats|Normal Cat]], this unit suffers from a severe lack of good basic stats, making him underperform greatly in his field. For this reason, usage of this unit, especially prior to unlocking his True Form, is not recommended.

==='''True Form'''===
Li'l Jamiera Cat's usage is the same as [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Jamiera Cat]]'s, as his stats become similar and he gains the same ability. Despite having a faster attack animation, his stats remain considerably lower than his normal counterpart, making him never worth using as a replacement and limiting his usage greatly compared to Jamiera, a unit who already has few applications.

==='''Talents'''===
Even with Attack Up and HP Up Talents, Li'l Jamiera's stats are not that special. However, in {{4c}} stages, these stats become more serviceable.

The [[Shield Piercing]] Talent isn't worth getting either. Due to Li'l Jamiera's short range and rather long attack animation, getting his attacks to connect properly on said aggressive threats is next to impossible, and a successful Shield Pierce would be nothing short of a miracle.

On the other hand, [[Immune to Weaken|Weaken Immune]] is situational at best and just isn't worth the cost, since he again just can't hit them. Meanwhile, [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Cyborg Cat]] doesn't need NP to gain Weaken Immunity, and dishes out damage at a safer range. Similarly, Surge Resist doesn't do enough, as enemy surge attacks often do extreme damage and cutting it in half doesn't help much.

{{Job|Classification = Tanker & Melee}}

